WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions of "Electron Transport Chain" by Drew Berry, wehi.tv, for HHMI BioInteractive, from the film's page on YouTube (youtu.be/zNpeuA4gtq0).
Each cue is one line here, and mishearings in the captions are put right (plans/follow-the-molecule/captions.py lists them).

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.290
The center of activity that brings your cells to life

2
00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:10.180
is found inside the dynamic mitochondria organelle.

3
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.580
The inner mitochondrial membrane is

4
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:16.720
coated with enzymes that catalyze the chemical reactions

5
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.950
of respiration, working in sequence to generate

6
00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.850
the electron transport chain.

7
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.100
The first step in the electron transport chain

8
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:32.820
is performed by enzyme complex 1.

9
00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:38.570
Complex 1 receives electrons from coenzyme NADH,

10
00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:43.520
a substrate produced by the citric acid cycle.

11
00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:47.380
The catalytic mechanism of enzyme complex 1

12
00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:51.710
connects two different kinds of reaction.

13
00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:57.410
Coenzyme NADH is oxidized at one end of the enzyme,

14
00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:01.280
releasing two electrons that hop through the interior

15
00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.724
to coenzyme Q, which is reduced.

16
00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:10.340
Traveling amongst membrane lipids,

17
00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:15.140
coenzyme Q carries electrons to the next step in the electron

18
00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:16.100
transport chain.

19
00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:24.820
The movement of charged electrons through complex 1

20
00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:28.360
makes it bend in shape, transmitting energy

21
00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:30.985
for pumping four protons across the membrane.

22
00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:46.880
The second step of the electron transport chain

23
00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:51.230
is performed by enzyme complex 3.

24
00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:54.800
The mechanism of complex 3 separates electrons

25
00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:58.550
from coenzyme Q, passing one electron

26
00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:00.980
to cytochrome c, which is reduced.

27
00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:13.850
A complete reaction cycle of enzyme complex 3

28
00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:18.500
transports four protons across the membrane.

29
00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:21.640
Traveling within the intermembrane space,

30
00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:24.980
reduced cytochrome c carries the electron

31
00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:30.240
to the final step in the electron transport chain.

32
00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:32.780
The destination for electron transport

33
00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:37.070
is a molecule of oxygen held inside enzyme complex four.

34
00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:44.620
Reduced cytochrome c delivers electrons

35
00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:48.970
that transfer to the reaction center of enzyme complex four.

36
00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:55.090
A molecule of oxygen from the air you breathe

37
00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:57.355
is captured, split, and reduced.

38
00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:03.690
The separated oxygen atoms accept electrons

39
00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:07.680
and pick up protons, creating two molecules of water.

40
00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:36.050
The substrate providing electrons to enzyme complex 1

41
00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:42.700
is coenzyme NADH, a product of the citric acid cycle.

42
00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:46.700
A second supply of electrons for the electron transport chain

43
00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:51.650
is from step 6 of the citric acid cycle, performed by enzyme

44
00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:54.620
complex 2.

45
00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:59.690
Enzyme complex 2 catalyzes oxidation of succinate,

46
00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:02.930
releasing two electrons which hop through the enzyme

47
00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:05.480
to coenzyme Q, which is reduced.

48
00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:13.570
Traveling through the membrane, coenzyme Q

49
00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:17.860
carries the electron to enzyme complex 3 of the electron

50
00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:20.040
transport chain.
